  "summary": "Mwana pwo masks, cihongo thunder god and carved thrones of the Chokwe court style.",
  "description": "Chokwe carvers served a court culture born of the Lunda empire's expansion: mwana pwo female masks with filed-teeth beauty marks and braided wigs danced fertility; cihongo masks with jutting chin and white face embodied the thunder-chief Chihongo collecting tribute; thrones, stools and footrests carried incised cosmograms and seated chiefs in trade-cloth splendor. Chokwe ivory, ironwork and the divination basket ngombo ya cisuka spread the style across three modern countries, and collectors rank its carving among Africa's great court arts.",
